# Node.js Backend Deployment — AWS EC2

## Live Projects
- haven.thukool.online
- secret.thukool.online

## Stack
- AWS EC2 (Ubuntu 24.04)
- Node.js + PM2 (process management)
- Nginx (reverse proxy)
- Let's Encrypt / Certbot (SSL)
- GitHub Webhooks (CI/CD auto-deployment)

## Architecture
GitHub push → Webhook triggers EC2 → 
Script pulls latest code → PM2 restarts app → 
Nginx routes traffic → SSL termination

## What Was Configured
- EC2 instance provisioned and secured
- Nginx configured as reverse proxy for two separate backends on same server
- SSL certificates issued via Certbot for both subdomains
- PM2 configured to auto-restart on crash and persist across reboots
- GitHub webhook CI/CD — push to main branch auto-deploys without manual SSH

## Key Skills Demonstrated
- Linux server administration
- Reverse proxy configuration
- SSL/TLS certificate management
- CI/CD pipeline setup
- Process management
